sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch08-26> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Pigmentation patterns on mollusc shells are produced line by line by pigment-secreting elements whose new states depend on neighbors' previous states, so the range of shell patterns closely matches the patterns of the simplest symmetric one-dimensional cellular automata.";
    dc:type "model-of-nature";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mollusc shell pigment patterns are generated like one-dimensional cellular automata";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 8, “Implications for Everyday Systems”; section “Biological Pigmentation Patterns” (from p. 422), p. 425. Scope: pigmentation patterns on mollusc shells"
}
